== AGGREGATE: 0 PASS, 64 SIGNED of 64 stabilizer streams ==
   rank-scan: 2/64 streams show a resample-stable complex pair at any order <= 3; 0/64 show a stable pair that is also DOMINANT (median |z|/rho >= 0.95) - the clock signature (the oscillatory control shows dom 1.00)
   Bonferroni(64 tests, 5% family, x1.6 margins): ALL SIGNED SURVIVE (worst inflated upper bound -1.67e-05)
   top-moment run counts p(1^7): min 2, median 96, max 399

== controls ==
  iid control (rate 0.153):       lam_min -1.53e-05  CI [-2.92e-05, +5.33e-05]  cx-scan: none stable  -> PASS (moment-compatible)
  oscillatory control (same rate):    lam_min -9.40e-04  CI [-1.03e-03, -8.47e-04]  poles: rank 1 |Im|/|p| 0.000  cx-scan: r2: stab 0.90 dom 1.00 phase 0.08pi; r3: stab 1.00 dom 1.00 phase 0.29pi  -> SIGNED (no reversible Moore-form HMM)

  (the instrument: a hidden irrational rotation SIGNS the
   Hankel at matched rate and statistics, while iid passes -
   whatever the device data shows is therefore a statement
   about the device, not about the test's power)
